    "industrial_process_notes": "Chitin was first isolated in 1799 by Charles Hatchett; deacetylated chitin was named 'chitosan' in 1894 by Felix Hoppe-Seyler. Commercial production deacetylates chitin using excess sodium hydroxide in water, giving average molecular weights of 3,800-20,000 Da. Renewed research interest emerged in the 1970s driven by shellfish-waste disposal regulations.",
